tions":["Robert \"Waajid\" O'Bryant","Waadjeed","Waajid","Wajeed"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/175150-Waajeed","type":"artist","urls":["https://waajeed.bandcamp.com/","https://www.facebook.com/waajeedmusic/","http://instagram.com/jeedox","https://www.liaisonartists.com/artists/waajeed","http://myspace.com/waajeedandthebling47group","http://soundcloud.com/jeedo_x","http://twitter.com/Jeedo_X","http://www.whosampled.com/Waajeed/","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waajeed"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/18222225/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"18222225","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:18222225","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/18222225-Moemiki","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/2091172/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2091172","image":"https://i.discogs.com/dIuo-AdIrh-WOj7Trz-gbNKj9-EiGvCAVw7L69suKYM/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:500/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIwOTEx/NzItMTY0NjE3ODcx/NS05NTQ2LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/WxIc1r45WIXCjGna3B8BzRkHVNI5MpgticfMpXWhHCw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIwOTEx/NzItMTY0NjE3ODcx/NS05NTQ2LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"[url=https://www.discogs.com/de/style/kwaito]Kwaito[/url] band from South Africa\r\n\r\nMashamplani was originally formed by [a=M'Du] along with [url=https://www.discogs.com/de/artist/1267569-Tokollo-Tshabalala]Tokollo Magesh[/url], [a=S'Bu] and Pro Ngubane in 1995. They released the EP \"Hey Kop\" in 1995 and earned a reputation in the kwaito scene, especially with \"Is Fokol Is Niks\". The group disbanded the following year and got re-arranged by M'Du along with Tshidiso, Peppa, Mjakes, and Tumi and established a new \"Mashamplani 2\" project for the album \"Kunjalo Kunjalo\" in 1996. In 1997, they released \"Lost 'N Found\" with the notoriously diss tracks aimed at Tokollo, who decided to join [a=TKZee] later. Three more albums followed with a compilation CD \"Back 2 Square\" which featured their milestone hits.\r\n\r\nTumi passed away in September 2010.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:2091172","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":1087525,"name":"Mduduzi Masilela"},{"active":true,"id":1267569,"name":"Tokollo Tshabalala"},{"active":true,"id":2959170,"name":"S'bu"}],"namevariations":["Mashamplani 2","Mojalifa"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/2091172-Mashamplani","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/2207552/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2207552","image":"https://i.discogs.com/hA7PW_xGaIcLMRfLI8Ei8hiZwIMlG2k8DuQnbboqzws/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:377/w:567/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIyMDc1/NTItMTM3Njc0NDk4/OS0zODU4LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/IbN84Cm6lyX_GRDYDGLHq47j8mkPvGGnctGCjiqMAYc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIyMDc1/NTItMTM3Njc0NDk4/OS0zODU4LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"British MC born in Spanish Town, Jamaica, in 1985. Relocated to London in 2000.\r\nSon of [a=D. McDermott] aka [a=Poison Chang]. Brother of [a=Kodi Starr].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:2207552","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":781284,"name":"Jason McDermott"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["MC Stylo G","Stylo","Stylo G.","Stylo-G"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/2207552-Stylo-G","type":"artist","urls":["http://stylog.co.uk/","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stylo_G"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/2366/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2366","image":"https://i.discogs.com/DtS_A-XpwCSerdGeuZyFIjvRDMkwzTUag98WYuSplqE/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:471/w:456/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIzNjYt/MTIxNDk2MjE2Ni5q/cGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/jBcsQSVPQsyknEWCUV3qlrX_YviTTpfnAqtQ_iIRCeY/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIzNjYt/MTIxNDk2MjE2Ni5q/cGVn.jpeg","profile":"American DJ/producer and emcee from Chicago, born 1979.\r\nGant Garrard (pronounced Jerrod)  is a disc jockey who was introduced to mixing in the early 1980s by his older brother and learned how to count beats and blend records at the young age of 5 with hip hop, New York garage, Chicago house, electronic and disco music.\r\n\r\nAt age 10 he was ready to share his talent with the world and began mixing on a college radio station in Chicago WKKC 89.3 FM where he mixed from 1989 through 1997. At age 15 in 1995, Gant produced his first EP for Dance Mania called \"It's About Time\" which spawned the Chicago Underground smash \"3 Blind Mice\", which was built around the theme music from The Three Stooges television show. He became known in Chicago as the Youngest Professional DJ and is attributed to being one of the main key innovators of Ghetto Juke House.\r\n\r\nAt age 18 he began to travel, playing both the Rave and club circuits in the U.S. as well as in Europe. In 1998-99 Gant was playing in Paris at Le Queen and Gibus as well as in Geneva, Switzerland at the Lake Parade prepared him for his Summer 2000 residency in Ibiza, Spain at El Divino alongside Paul Johnson and DJ Skip. You Gotta Get Up was a huge success on Dust Traxx Chicago that was even reissued with Paul Johnson remixes and continues to be repressed due to relentless demand. Gant has recently teamed with 2004 Grammy award winning producer Maurice Joshua to work on remix production for Beyoncé, Destiny's Child and other major artists as well as submitting Juke House remixes to major labels hoping the A&R's will give Gant a chance to exploit this long awaited underground Chicago sound that has been around since 1992.\r\n\r\nAs of December 2005, Gant is the first DJ/producer to have a Chicago Juke house remix for a major artist on a major label with his remix for Beyonce's \"Check On It\" featuring Slim Thug on Columbia/Sony Records. For the past couple of years multi-talented Gant has silently leaked his hip hop producing skills to the rap industry. 2006 his Juke remix of \"Shake & Pop\" is one of highest downloaded tracks in Juke House music. 2007 Gant-Man teamed with A-Trak and new artist Kid Sister and released Control/Damn Girl Juke Remix. Now with 17 years of being a DJ, 12 years of producing tracks and releasing production on labels like Columbia, Riviera, Dust Traxx, Treehouse, Bunchlox, R&R Records, Fools Gold, and Dance Mania, his career has become more prolific with each passing year. He is one of the up and coming producers to watch in 2008. Gant has the experience to move crowds all over the world with his House, Ghetto Juke, old school & Hip-Hop sound and will move any crowd he is given the chance to.\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:2366","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":2180,"name":"Gant Garrard"},{"id":1413147,"name":"Garrard Wilson"},{"id":2619429,"name":"The Youngest Professional D.J."}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["D.J. Gant-Man","DJ Gant","DJ Gant Man","DJ Gant-Man","DJ Gant-man","DJ Gant-man Wilson","DJ Gantman","DJ Gentman","Gant","Gant \"Man\"","Gant Man","Gant-Man Wilson","Gantman"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/2366-Gant-Man","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.myspace.com/djgantman","http://www.myspace.com/gantgarrard","https://www.linkedin.com/in/gant-man-garrard-00337719","https://soundcloud.com/djgant-man"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/2785317/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2785317","image":"https://i.discogs.com/9wzcTLCWxfSqr3zKIs9xA-UvGDfMPzMYbvW2NuhuOaU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:534/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI3ODUz/MTctMTQxMzIwMTY1/MS04NDE4LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/-vHtyqoJ5B3oqMELXBsyrJ0j7Fe66Cnub0C6JQF0fGU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI3ODUz/MTctMTQxMzIwMTY1/MS04NDE4LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Borrowed Identity is widely recognised as a chameleon within the electronic music scene. He can tastefully and strategically mix various forms of house, techno and disco depending on his reaction to the environment and the crowd, expanding his skills towards a more freestyle manner if he feels is appropriate for the occasion.\r\n\r\nLikewise, the multi-disciplinary DJ who helms from Berlin, Germany, can provide a truly focussed direction for the crowd and the dance floor, opting for those present to completely let go and have a good time. Instead of limiting himself to one genre to create an easy to promote image as a DJ he attempts with every show to catch the appropriate vibe in each club, going with the motions of the crowd as they motion with him.\r\n\r\nBorrowed Identity is wise beyond his years, having played many of the most renowned clubs in Europe such as Berghain/Panorama Bar, Concrete, Fabric and shows further afield in the likes of Asia, Australia and Canada. Besides his DJ-ing credentials he has released numerous music on labels such as Lets Play House, Quintessentials, Mistress as well as remixing for Ben Sims, Jacques Renault, Max Graef, Luke Solomon and many more.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:2785317","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/2785317-Borrowed-Identity","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.facebook.com/Borrowed.Identity/","http://soundcloud.com/borrowed-identity","http://www.residentadvisor.net/dj/borrowedidentity"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/37757/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"37757","image":"https://i.discogs.com/zhabEIaJGxAxcd9GopUlKOgewvSIQ2KTzIF1ol9ZnsY/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM3NzU3/LTE3Mzk5MTQwNTIt/OTIzMC5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/p6UmCmwL06cfkFKuEjgw5n0ZX9vH6S_Z7wrOU6F02HQ/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM3NzU3/LTE3Mzk5MTQwNTIt/OTIzMC5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Norwegian band formed in Oslo in 1982. The band split in 2010 after a worldwide tour of 73 shows.\r\nIn December 2014 they announced they would participate in the \"Rock in Rio\" festival for September 2015.\r\nIn March 2015 they announced a comeback album \"Cast In Steel\" that was released September of that year. The first single from that album \"Under The Makeup\" was released in July 2015.\r\nThey continue to record and tour.\r\n\r\nMorten Harket (born September 14th, 1959): vocals\r\nPaul Waaktaar-Savoy (born September 6th, 1961): guitar, vocals\r\nMagne Furuholmen (born November 1st, 1962): keyboards, vocals","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:37757","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":147679,"name":"Magne Furuholmen"},{"active":true,"id":333419,"name":"Morten Harket"},{"active":true,"id":634036,"name":"Paul Waaktaar-Savoy"}],"namevariations":["A - H A","A - HA","A - Ha","A - ha","A HA","A Ha","A ha","A – Ha","A- ha","A-HA","A-Ha","A-Ha!","A-Ha合唱團","A-ha!","A. Ha","A1","AA-HA","AH HA","AHA","Ah-Ha","Aha","a - ha","a ha","a-ah","a-ha: Harket, Waaktaar-Savoy & Furuholmen","a-ha合唱團","aha","a~ha","a·ha","А-ХA","啊哈合唱團","阿哈合唱團","아-하","아하"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/37757-a-ha","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.a-ha.com","http://a-ha-live.com","http://www.discog.info/a-ha.html","http://www.facebook.com/officialaha","http://myspace.com/aha","http://twitter.com/aha_com","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A-ha","https://www.allmusic.com/artist/a-ha-mn0000480108"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/4890424/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"4890424","image":"https://i.discogs.com/fVbWuYA6yuoOyzA40uvej8FDvMgyS-d-Bwa-mAksKBc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:483/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ4OTA0/MjQtMTc3NzQ2NjMz/Mi0yMTMzLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/a0b7zfHDgRTkqEDjPJYqDv0sPildVm1S1cxZFh8MZOE/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ4OTA0/MjQtMTc3NzQ2NjMz/Mi0yMTMzLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Kassian is an exploration of Techno, Bass and Electronica from London duo Warren Cummings and Joe Danvers. Since forming in 2019, they’ve evolved from groove-heavy house roots into a forward-thinking club act with releases on !K7, Heist, Phonica and Shall Not Fade. Their imprint Faux Poly has become a respected outlet in its own right, now reaching its 20th release — a new Kassian EP marking their return to the label. Their music continues to draw support from leading selectors including Ben UFO, Four Tet, Floating Points, Caribou and Dixon.\n\nFollowing their Phase Two and Supercontinent EPs on !K7 — the latter spotlighting standout cuts Yena and Pulgueiro Baile — Kassian released their debut album Channels in 2025 to widespread acclaim, including praise from Pitchfork. The duo have built a global reputation through appearances at Panorama Bar, Watergate, Love International and Kala, alongside tours across the US, Canada, Australia, New Zealand and most recently India. Their long-running Rinse FM residency continues to showcase their evolving sound and deep connection to London’s electronic scene.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:4890424","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":6081362,"name":"Warren Luke Cummings"},{"active":true,"id":6788112,"name":"Joe Danvers"}],"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/4890424-Kassian","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.facebook.com/kassiansound/","https://soundcloud.com/kassiansound"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/6336795/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"6336795","image":"https://i.discogs.com/KA91qoxnrs-vwmXWiXkzwwxGvH2GlxIesMEgxSGtfNM/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:449/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTYzMzY3/OTUtMTUzNzk5MzA3/Ni01ODI4LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/1JrZoi5tp25jANpmMIkp